## Closing answer

"I separate `Book`, the catalogue title, from `BookItem`, the physical copy with a barcode and status. Members have a `MembershipPlan` with their limits, loan length, renewals and fine rate, so new plans need no new classes. `LibraryService` is the single place that lends: checkout checks the member's limit and the copy's status in one synchronized step. Return closes the loan, calculates the fine with calendar dates, and gives the copy to the first waiting hold for that title with a two-day pickup window; a daily job passes uncollected copies on. Renewal extends the same loan unless someone is waiting."
